SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"DR Congo: State Mining Company Subject to a Damning Audit","publisher":"OCCRP","publication_date":"2022","url":"https://www.occrp.org/en/news/dr-congo-state-mining-company-subject-to-a-damning-audit","claim":"OCCRP reports that the anti-corruption agency found severe irregularities, including embezzlement, at state mining company Gecamines that deprived the state budget of hundreds of millions of dollars.","locator":"lead paragraph","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct reporting on an audit by the anti-corruption agency; the finding is attributed to the audit and is specific, though the article is reporting rather than the audit text itself.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022; directly relevant to Tshisekedi-era governance and mining-sector integrity","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but meaningful: the audit concerns a state enterprise under Tshisekedi's government, not a personal act by Tshisekedi himself.","contrary_evidence":["The article does not prove personal enrichment by Tshisekedi or his family.","It is an audit-based allegation rather than a court finding in the article itself."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"DR Congo: State Mining Company Subject to a Damning Audit","publisher":"OCCRP","publication_date":"2022","url":"https://www.occrp.org/en/news/dr-congo-state-mining-company-subject-to-a-damning-audit","claim":"The same OCCRP report says the audit was commissioned in September 2021 by President Felix Tshisekedi, who had pledged to scrutinize and renegotiate mining agreements closed under his predecessor.","locator":"paragraph beginning 'The audit was commissioned in September last year'","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct statement of a presidential action reported by OCCRP; the commissioning is specific and ruler-attributable, though the article is secondary reporting.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"retrospective but relevant to 2022 because it shows an anti-corruption oversight step taken by Tshisekedi before and during the target year","ruler_attribution":"Direct: Tshisekedi is named as the commissioner of the audit.","contrary_evidence":["Commissioning an audit does not show the audit was effective.","The article also reports severe corruption at the enterprise, limiting the strength of the positive inference."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"The Democratic Republic of the Congo has achieved a high overall score in implementing the 2019 EITI Standard","publisher":"EITI","publication_date":"2022","url":"https://eiti.org/board-decision/2022-50","claim":"EITI says that in the 2018-2020 reporting cycle only 21 of 77 extractive licensees with significant revenues submitted beneficial ownership information, and that the legal framework for beneficial ownership disclosures was still incomplete.","locator":"sections 2.5.3 and 2.5 assessment lines 449-453","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent international transparency body, specific numerical disclosure gap, and a clear locator in the validation decision.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022; the validation decision evaluates disclosure practices that were current in the target-period governance environment","ruler_attribution":"Indirect: this is sector transparency under Tshisekedi's government rather than a personal act, but it reflects the integrity environment around extractive governance.","contrary_evidence":["The same decision notes the DRC achieved a high overall score on implementation.","This does not by itself show Tshisekedi personally concealed ownership or profited."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Des proches de Tshisekedi accusés de corruption","publisher":"Deutsche Welle","publication_date":"2022-09-22","url":"https://www.dw.com/fr/rdc-corruption-vital-kamerhe-eteni-longondo-vidiye-tshimanga-f%C3%A9lix-tshisekedi/a-63211185","claim":"DW reports that several close associates of Tshisekedi were accused of corruption or embezzlement, and that Tshisekedi had not yet reacted to these cases at the time of publication.","locator":"paragraphs 44-52","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"The article is a reputable international outlet summarizing multiple named corruption allegations, but it remains a secondary report over a cluster of cases involving associates rather than Tshisekedi personally.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022; directly within the target year and about Tshisekedi's governing circle","ruler_attribution":"Indirect: the allegations concern close associates, ministers, and party figures in Tshisekedi's orbit; no direct proof of Tshisekedi's personal knowledge or benefit is supplied here.","contrary_evidence":["The article does not establish Tshisekedi's personal participation in the alleged corruption.","Some named figures were later acquitted or denied wrongdoing."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.7","7B.9","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"DR Congo: No Inquiry into Police Role in Ethnic Killings","publisher":"Human Rights Watch","publication_date":"2022-05-23","url":"https://www.hrw.org/news/2022/05/23/dr-congo-no-inquiry-police-role-ethnic-killings","claim":"HRW says Congolese authorities had not meaningfully investigated police involvement in the Buhene killings, and that after martial law came into force President Tshisekedi appointed the police commander in charge of the attacks as deputy territory administrator.","locator":"paragraphs 607-608 and 654","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"HRW gives a dated, specific account with named officials and a clear attribution chain to the president's appointment decision.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022, with retrospective reference to April 2021 events that shaped 2022 accountability choices","ruler_attribution":"Direct for the appointment and indirect for the failure to investigate; the article ties both to Tshisekedi-era authorities.","contrary_evidence":["The underlying violence began in 2021, so the failure is partly inherited.","The article does not prove Tshisekedi personally ordered the non-investigation."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"RDC : Félix Tshisekedi encourage le gouvernement à récupérer le patrimoine immobilier de l’État acquis indûment par des tiers","publisher":"Radio Okapi","publication_date":"2022-09-17","url":"https://www.radiookapi.net/2022/09/17/actualite/politique/rdc-felix-tshisekedi-encourage-le-gouvernement-recuperer-le","claim":"Radio Okapi reports that Tshisekedi urged the government to recover state real estate acquired unlawfully by third parties and to ensure transparency and respect for the law.","locator":"paragraph beginning 'Le Président Félix Antoine Tshisekedi a encouragé...'","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"The report quotes a specific presidential instruction from a mainstream Congolese outlet, but it is still official rhetoric rather than proof of execution.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"2022; direct ruler statement during the target year","ruler_attribution":"Direct: the quotation is attributed to Tshisekedi at a cabinet meeting.","contrary_evidence":["This is a promise or instruction, not proof of implementation.","The report does not show whether the recovery campaign succeeded or was selective."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.8","7B.10"]}

Search ledger:
- Candidates found: about 54 plausible documents across the query families I ran.
- Documents opened: 17 accessible documents in this wave before hitting browsing limits.
- Duplicate families removed: 14.
- Irrelevant or out-of-period items: 8.
- Inaccessible items: 3, mostly IMF eLibrary pages that returned 403.
- Accepted distinct URLs used in this dossier: 11.

Material gaps and next best directions:
- There is still no direct, ruler-specific asset-declaration or beneficial-ownership record for Tshisekedi himself in 2022.
- I still lack a clean primary source on campaign finance, presidential asset filings, or a court/audit record tying personal or family enrichment directly to Tshisekedi.
- Strong next sources would be:
  1. `Cour des comptes` and `IGF` audit reports on the presidency, ministries, and SOEs.
  2. Asset-declaration records for the president and cabinet, if available.
  3. Procurement and mining-contract registers tied to presidential appointees.
  4. Any court filings or sanctions findings on close presidential associates that explicitly discuss Tshisekedi's knowledge, benefit, or protection.
